# The build context is copied wholesale by `COPY . .`, so anything left here
# ends up in the image. Two reasons that matters:
#
#   .env    bakes every secret into an image layer, where it survives even if
#           the file is deleted in a later step.
#   .venv   is 400 MB of a laptop's Linux virtualenv that pip immediately
#           reinstalls anyway — pure build time and image size.

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.env
*.sqlite3
db.sqlite3
staticfiles/
celerybeat-schedule*
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
